<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Auto Backup rules for API 23-30 (API 31+ uses data_extraction_rules.xml,
    which must be kept in step with this file).

    `auth.xml` is the EncryptedSharedPreferences file behind AuthStore. Its
    contents are wrapped by an AndroidKeyStore master key, and **keystore keys
    are never backed up** — so restoring this file onto a new device (or after a
    reinstall) hands Tink a keyset it cannot decrypt, and every read throws
    AEADBadTagException. That crashed the app at launch, on the very first
    `isSignedIn` check, with no way out but clearing app data.

    Excluding it costs the user one sign-in after a restore, which is what
    happens anyway: a token that cannot be decrypted is not a session.

    `coaching.xml` holds at most one parked coaching-invite token (NS-38,
    PendingInvite): a single-use secret for the minutes between opening a link
    signed out and signing in. It has no business in a backup.

    `push.xml` is this install's coach-comment notification choice (NS-54,
    PushPrefs): a restored "on" would claim notifications on a phone that has
    never registered a token or been asked for the permission.

    `clips/` (files) holds best-lap video clips waiting to upload and the
    JSON manifest of their upload jobs (NS-45, ClipManifest). A clip is
    hundreds of MB, and a restored manifest pointing at a clip that wasn't
    restored with it is a dead job.

    `ai_coach.xml` is the EncryptedSharedPreferences file behind AICoachKeys
    (#320): the driver's own Anthropic / OpenAI / Gemini API keys for the AI Coach.
    A key the driver pays for must not follow a restore onto another device
    silently — and, like auth.xml, its keystore key never travels with it.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="auth.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="coaching.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="push.xml" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="clips/" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="ai_coach.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
